      "id": "C1",
      "severity": "hard-gate",
      "description": "Address-join hit rate is THRESHOLD-MARGINAL at ~28%, BELOW the implicit 30% kill line. Worse, the v0 plan does not specify the pre-join filter pipeline (drop APTNUM!='', drop STATE!='FL', drop HOMELESS/PO BOX, drop multifamily parcels). Without those filters, address-bound rate collapses to 12-18% AND the surviving joins point at LLC/REIT-owned apartment buildings — useless owner-mismatch leads. The plan's join key (bookingAddressNormalized == situsAddressNormalized) also omits ZIP+countyFips composite, which is required because DOR situsCity uses USPS-preferred names that don't match jurisdiction.",
      "fix": "Before B1, add to normalize.ts: (a) hard-filter APTNUM!='' (or store but mark non-joinable), (b) filter STATE!='FL', (c) drop /^P\\.?O\\.?\\s*BOX/i and HOMELESS/TRANSIENT/blank STREET, (d) join key = (countyFips=12095, normalizedStreet, zip5) with city as tiebreaker only. Also separate funnel into 'address-bound' vs 'owner-confirmed' stages — only the latter is a sellable lead. Re-probe 200-500 real bookings BEFORE B2 to convert hit-rate from low→medium confidence."
    },
    {
      "id": "C2",
      "severity": "hard-gate",
      "description": "The +15 boost applied at approve-time is NOT idempotent and NOT additive across signals. Per promote-idempotency check: if a parcel was already promoted via tax-delinquent path (dataSource='parcel-lien-bridge'), the bond-distress approve will overwrite dataSource and either double-boost (if naively added) or wipe the tax-delinquent signal (if score is recalculated standalone). Re-approving the same parcel will also re-apply +15.",
      "fix": "Refactor calculateDistressScoreFromProperty to accept a signals bag {taxDelinquent, bondDistress, foreclosure, ...} and compute score from the UNION of booleans currently true on the Property. Add Property.bondDistress:Boolean (or similar boolean signal flags). On approve: OR-merge bondDistress=true (never false), append 'bond-distress-manual' to dataSource CSV if not present, recompute from union. This is idempotent (recomputing twice = same score) and additive."
    },
    {
      "id": "C3",
      "severity": "hard-gate",
      "description": "Approve route's 'Property already exists' path is undefined. Per scenario 1+2 of promote-idempotency: the existing /api/properties/promote update branch does NOT touch dataSource, so bond-distress provenance is invisible on update. If approve mirrors promote verbatim, it inherits this bug. Also, re-booking of same inmate at same parcel creates Review #2; approving #2 without checking 'prior approved review for (userId, propertyId) already applied boost' causes double-count.",
      "fix": "Per recommendedApproveLogic in pre-check: if review.status==='approved' AND promotedPropertyId set, return existing Property without re-running score logic. On first approve, upsert on (userId,address,city,state,zip); CREATE branch sets bondDistress=true and computes score from signals; UPDATE branch OR-merges bondDistress, appends to dataSource CSV, recomputes from union. Wrap in $transaction with 60000ms timeout per CLAUDE.md."
    },
    {
      "id": "C4",
      "severity": "hard-gate",
      "description": "bondAmount as nullable Float is lossy for currency. OCFL returns '1000.00' as plain string — parsing to Float introduces IEEE-754 rounding (0.1+0.2 problem) and breaks downstream sum aggregations. The refuted-design summary explicitly called for Decimal/cents encoding.",
      "fix": "Schema: bondAmountCents Int? (parse as Math.round(parseFloat(str)*100)). OR use Prisma Decimal(12,2). Never Float for money. This is a B1 schema decision — cannot be fixed cheaply later because changing column type on a populated table requires backfill."
    },
    {
      "id": "C5",
      "severity": "soft",
      "description": "BondDistressReview as 1:1 with Record (unique FK on bondDistressRecordId) prevents re-review after a Reject. Scenario: operator rejects, later discovers inmate's address was a typo and wants to re-review. Schema forbids it. Also, scenario 3 of promote-idempotency flagged that there is no Unapprove path — a misclick approves forever.",
      "fix": "Drop the @unique on bondDistressRecordId; allow multiple reviews per record ordered by createdAt. Add 'superseded' status. Add an 'Unapprove' action that sets review.status back to 'pending', nulls promotedPropertyId, and either deletes the Property (if no user edits made) or archives it via Property.archivedAt:DateTime?. Scope all property lists to WHERE archivedAt IS NULL."
    },
    {
      "id": "C6",
      "severity": "soft",
      "description": "Match-candidate score formula (0.6+0.3+0.1) produces useless 0.1 floor noise when only countyFips matches — every OCFL record matches county 12095 trivially, so the UI will show 'top 3 candidates' that are random parcels in Orange County. This wastes operator attention.",
      "fix": "Add floor: only return candidates with score >= 0.3 (i.e. at least name OR address must hit). Drop the +0.1 county weight entirely since county is a precondition, not a signal. If <3 candidates clear floor, return fewer + show 'manual APN entry' input."
    },
    {
      "id": "C7",
      "severity": "soft",
      "description": "Property → BondDistressRecord linkage via metadata JSON (implied) is the wrong call. Promoted Property loses queryable backlink to source record; can't answer 'how many properties were promoted from bond distress this month' without JSON scans.",
      "fix": "Add Review.promotedPropertyId FK (already in plan — good). Also add Property.sourceBondDistressRecordId Int? FK for direct backlink. Index it. JSON metadata is fine for raw provenance dump but not for queryable joins."
    },
    {
      "id": "C8",
      "severity": "soft",
      "description": "No row-claim / lock mechanism. Two operators clicking Approve simultaneously on same review = data race; both create Properties (different userIds = OK per scenario 4) OR same-userId double-approve creates two Properties via upsert race. Unique (userId,address,city,state,zip) saves us in DB but the second request errors confusingly.",
      "fix": "Add Review.claimedBy:String? + claimedAt:DateTime? with 15-min TTL. Queue endpoint sets claim atomically (UPDATE ... WHERE claimedBy IS NULL OR claimedAt < now-15min). Approve endpoint checks claimedBy === session.userId. v0 single-operator is acceptable to defer, but flag as known limitation in spec."
    },
    {
      "id": "C9",
      "severity": "hard-gate",
      "description": "middleware.ts /app(.*) public bypass means /app/admin/bond-distress page has ZERO server-side auth. The plan assumes API gating is enough, but admin UI pages will render to any user (including unauthenticated) until they call the API.",
      "fix": "Per admin-role-gating check: extract requireAdmin() helper to lib/auth/require-admin.ts; add explicit non-public matcher in middleware.ts for /app/admin(.*) and /api/admin(.*); move ADMIN_EMAIL to process.env. +1.5h to B3 budget. This is a prerequisite, not optional."
    }
  ],
  "summary": "Plan is REFUTED in current form. Five hard-gate correctness defects block B1: (1) address-join hit rate is marginal and the plan omits the filter pipeline needed to hit 30%; (2) the flat +15 boost is non-idempotent and conflicts with existing tax-delinquent provenance; (3) the approve route inherits the existing promote route's dataSource-overwrite bug; (4) bondAmount as Float is lossy for currency and locks in a bad schema; (5) admin UI has no middleware gate. Softer issues — 1:1 review constraint, county-only candidate noise, missing FK backlink, no row claim — can wait for B3/B4 but should be tracked. Recommend SHRINK + HARDEN: re-probe 200 bookings before B2, refactor scoring to signals-bag before B1 schema lock, encode bondAmount as Int cents, fix middleware before any admin route ships. Do not start B1 until C1-C4 and C9 are resolved in the spec."
}

