    {
      "id": "L1-counsel-gate",
      "severity": "kill",
      "description": "Outside-counsel sign-off is downgraded from B0 hard-gate (refuted design) to a 'pre-build question' in v0. No evidence sign-off was acquired. Building B1-B6 (~48h) produces dead code that cannot be turned on. Worse: a paper trail of 'we built it before we cleared it' is itself discoverable in any future plaintiff suit.",
      "fix": "Re-instate B0 as hard-gate: written memo from FL-licensed counsel covering §119.071(4)(d), §119.071(2)(j) (victim info), Marsy's Law (Art. I §16(b)), FDUTPA §501.204 (deceptive trade re neutral-copy framing), TCPA if any outreach to inmate phones. Memo must be in repo at /legal/ocfl-counsel-memo-YYYY-MM-DD.pdf BEFORE B1 schema push. Estimated $3-6k flat fee, 1-2 weeks turnaround."
    },
    {
      "id": "L2-chapter-suppression",
      "severity": "block",
      "description": "v0 plan has ZERO charge-chapter suppression. §741 (domestic violence), §784.046 (repeat violence / dating / sexual viol. protective orders), §794 (sexual battery), §800 (lewd/lascivious), §827 (child abuse): victim/petitioner address and identity are statutorily confidential. Even if the inmate is the perpetrator, charge text can re-identify the victim and victim residence — which is often the booking address. Charges getCharges returns CHAPTER-NUMBERED strings; this is a hard filter we can implement, and shipping without it is a §119 violation per booking.",
      "fix": "Add chargeChapterFilter.ts: regex against /^(741|784\\.046|794|800|827|39\\.|92\\.56)/ on Charge field; drop ENTIRE booking (not just charge) if any matched charge present. Also drop where ArrestingAgency contains 'DCF' or 'CHILD PROTECTIVE'. Log suppressed count for audit. 4h."
    },
    {
      "id": "L3-mugshot-http-layer",
      "severity": "block",
      "description": "Plan says 'discard at parse, never persist' but getInmateDetails returns IMAGE inline as ~66KB base64 in the JSON body — by the time you parse JSON you've already downloaded it AND it's sat in node memory AND likely logged in any request-tracing middleware. Not HTTP-layer suppression.",
      "fix": "Two-step: (a) stream JSON parse and null-out IMAGE before object materializes (oboe.js or manual chunked parse), or (b) accept the download but ensure request-logger / Sentry breadcrumbs / BD proxy logs strip IMAGE field via redactor middleware. Verify with a header-only HEAD pre-flight if OCFL supports it. Add unit test asserting IMAGE never appears in any log transport. 6h."
    },
    {
      "id": "L4-pii-retention",
      "severity": "block",
      "description": "BondDistressRecord stores name+DOB+address for non-customers indefinitely. No purge endpoint, no retention TTL, no FDLE seal/expunge sync. FL §943.0585/0586 expunge orders require us to delete on receipt; without an ingest path for sealed-records lists, we silently violate sealing orders. CCPA/upcoming FL Digital Bill of Rights also implicate purge-on-request.",
      "fix": "Add (a) BondDistressRecord.purgeAfter: DateTime defaulting to capturedAt + 180d, (b) nightly cron purging where purgeAfter < now AND no associated approved BondDistressReview, (c) /api/admin/bond-distress/[id]/purge admin endpoint, (d) monthly FDLE seal/expunge list ingest (separate scraper, deferred but stub model). On Property promote, redact source PII — store only Parcel FK + 'bond-distress-manual' tag, never inmate name. 8h."
