      "severity": "block",
      "description": "150-250 bookings/day × (chapter-filter drops ~15%) × (out-of-FL drops 5%) × (apartment drops 35%) × (homeless/PO drops 8%) ≈ 70-130 reviewable/day. At 90s/review (read charges, eyeball 3 candidates, decide), that's 105-195 min/day = 1.75-3.25 hours/day of skilled-operator time, every day, indefinitely. Holidays/PTO = backlog explosion. Pre-build join-hit-rate of 28-32% assumed full triage; under load, operator cherrypicks easy joins and the marginal/orphan tail inflates the stated hit rate.",
      "fix": "(a) Set daily review SLA cap (top-50 by score, drop the rest with 24h TTL), (b) add 'defer' action that auto-purges in 7d, (c) instrument time-per-review and weekly throughput dashboard, (d) explicitly budget for a 0.25-FTE reviewer post-pilot. Pilot for 2 weeks before expanding."
